      "body": "Hi @Trinetra-MSFT Thx for response.  \r\n\r\n> Teams enables the Remove button after 5 seconds, even if your tab hasn't called setValidityState().\r\n\r\nThis is very strange. 5 seconds is a very short time. What's the point of having app's call setValidityState if it will have no effect after 5 seconds?\r\n\r\nI get that you probably want to allow end users to remove Tab regardless of app logic (like in case of app error). However, I feel either: \r\n1. That there should be an alternative mechanism for end user to hard remove tab\r\n2. Or, the documentation should not recommend app developers to call `setValidityState` as its confusing and has no ultimate effect. \r\n3. Or, There should be a longer timeout to enable the remove button. \r\n\r\nThx for your consideration",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
