      "created_at": "2020-01-23T03:07:56Z",
      "updated_at": "2020-01-23T03:07:56Z",
      "body": "Thanks for letting us know this. Is there documentation on this? Seems problematic. Companies will expect that uninstalling an app hard deletes all data. Imagine one user adds the app and installs several tabs. That user ends up leaving the org and the app is subsequently uninstalled. Then another user later installs the app...then all of the previous tabs are restored unbeknownst to the current user. In a team with a lot of channels, it would be near impossible to manage - let alone the compliance issues with the 3rd party app holding onto data it shouldn't (if the app is uninstalled).\r\n\r\nThere should be a full app uninstall hook that notifies the app to clean up all of its component references and data.",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
